linkmap_demo_intro = The linkmap addon replaces the classic linkmap popup with an overlay. This page shows every way to use it. Prefills are random articles of this installation; the addon ships no content of its own.
linkmap_demo_section_api = 1. Try the picker (JS API)
linkmap_demo_api_intro = This is how editors, modules and other addons call the picker. The result shows up here as a message.
linkmap_demo_pick_article = Pick an article
linkmap_demo_pick_articles = Pick several articles
linkmap_demo_pick_all = Pick an article or dataset
linkmap_demo_browse = Browse only
linkmap_demo_sources_hint = Datasets are only offered when the caller enables them with the sources option. Without it there are articles only, because the result must then be an article ID.
linkmap_demo_section_widget = 2. Widget for articles (lm-widget)
linkmap_demo_widget_intro = An input with the class lm-widget automatically becomes an article picker with name display. The article ID is stored, comma separated for multiple – compatible with REX_LINK, REX_LINKLIST and be_link.
linkmap_demo_widget_single = Single (empty)
linkmap_demo_widget_prefilled = Single (prefilled)
linkmap_demo_widget_multi = Multiple (max. 5)
linkmap_demo_section_classic = 3. Classic widgets (REX_LINK / REX_LINKLIST)
linkmap_demo_classic_intro = The core widgets stay unchanged – only the click on the linkmap icon now opens the overlay. The same applies to CKEditor 5, TinyMCE, MForm and Builder.
linkmap_demo_section_yform = 4. YForm and datasets
linkmap_demo_yform_unavailable = YForm is not installed – dataset picking and the YForm value types require YForm.
linkmap_demo_tableset_intro = Besides articles the picker can return datasets from YForm tables. To keep the examples meaningful for your installation they appear only after installing a small demo table set. It contains:
linkmap_demo_tableset_item_table = a YForm table "Linkmap Demo: REDAXO-News" with twelve sample news about REDAXO (title, teaser, category, date, status)
linkmap_demo_tableset_item_source = the release of this table as dataset source (System → Linkmap → Settings)
linkmap_demo_tableset_item_vu = two virtual_urls profiles (triggers /{0}/) so the scheme dialog for multiple URL profiles becomes visible – they only route these triggers to the start and 404 article
linkmap_demo_tableset_item_template = a URL template /redaxo-news/{id} for resolution (virtual_urls is not installed)
linkmap_demo_tableset_remove_hint = Everything can be removed here with one click. Do not install on production systems.
linkmap_demo_tableset_install = Install demo table set
linkmap_demo_tableset_uninstall = Remove demo table set
linkmap_demo_tableset_installed = Demo table set installed – the examples below now use the table "Linkmap Demo: REDAXO-News".
linkmap_demo_tableset_removed = Demo table set removed.
linkmap_demo_tableset_active = The demo table set is installed: table "{0}", enabled as dataset source.
linkmap_demo_scheme_hint_vu = The table has two virtual_urls profiles. Picking a single dataset therefore shows the "Choose URL scheme" dialog with preview URLs; multi select and relation mode choose the scheme automatically at render time.
linkmap_demo_scheme_hint_template = The table is resolved via the URL template /redaxo-news/{id} – simple demo. With the url addon or virtual_urls a profile-based resolution could be chosen at install time, showing the scheme dialog for multiple profiles.
linkmap_demo_sub_links = Datasets in the picker (link format)
linkmap_demo_sub_links_intro = Widgets in link format store links instead of IDs – the only way to keep articles and datasets in one field. Frontend URLs are generated by the addon at render time.
linkmap_demo_widget_link_single = Single (article or dataset)
linkmap_demo_widget_link = Multiple (articles and datasets mixed)
linkmap_demo_sub_relation = Relation mode (fixed table, dataset ID)
linkmap_demo_relation_intro = The field defines the table, only its datasets can be picked and the ID is stored – like be_manager_relation, but with the overlay. No structure, no URL resolution needed.
linkmap_demo_widget_relation = Single from "{0}"
linkmap_demo_widget_relation_multi = Multiple from "{0}"
linkmap_demo_sub_form = YForm form (value types linkmap and linkmap_relation)
linkmap_demo_yform_intro = Live form – submitting shows the stored values. The same fields exist in the table manager as field type "value".
linkmap_demo_yform_field_single = Target page (article)
linkmap_demo_yform_field_multi = Target pages (articles, max. 3)
linkmap_demo_yform_field_link_single = Target (article or dataset)
linkmap_demo_yform_field_link = Targets (articles and datasets)
linkmap_demo_yform_field_relation = Reference to "{0}" (relation)
linkmap_demo_yform_submitted = Form submitted – see values below.
linkmap_demo_resolver_label = URL resolution for the demo table
linkmap_demo_resolver_vu = virtual_urls: two profiles (triggers /{0}/) – shows the scheme dialog for multiple profiles
linkmap_demo_resolver_url = url addon: two profiles (namespaces {0}) – shows the scheme dialog for multiple profiles
linkmap_demo_resolver_template = URL template /redaxo-news/{id} only – simple demo without scheme choice
linkmap_demo_tableset_item_resolver = a URL resolution of your choice (see below); profiles only route their own triggers or namespaces to the start and 404 article
linkmap_demo_scheme_hint_url = The table has two url addon profiles. Picking a single dataset therefore shows the "Choose URL scheme" dialog with preview URLs; multi select and relation mode choose the scheme automatically at render time.
linkmap_tables_schemes_hint = Only checked schemes are offered in the picker and used at render time; none checked = all.
